 ## Overview
-This method enables interactive isosurface rendering on multi-core processors by combining object-order traversal with restricted ray casting [S1, unofficial]. It solves load-balancing and memory hierarchy overhead problems inherent in static screen partitioning by dynamically allocating ray casting tasks to threads while maintaining spatial locality [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that may use static grids or purely image-order traversal, this approach explicitly decouples the identification of candidate data blocks from the ray casting execution, using a two-phase process to restrict the search space to a small, front-to-back list of blocks per pixel [S1, unofficial].
